articles.body:
The content model of this starter lives in `gohead/model.json`. It describes locales, components, collections, singletons and what anonymous visitors may read.

```json
{
  "collections": {
    "articles": {
      "draftAndPublish": true,
      "attributes": {
        "title": { "type": "string", "required": true, "localized": true },
        "slug": { "type": "uid", "required": true, "unique": true }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Push it

```bash
npm run gohead:push
```

The CLI shows what changes, creates what is missing and updates what differs. It never deletes a collection, and it refuses to remove attributes unless you pass `--allow-removals`.

## Pull it

Changed the model in the admin UI? Bring it back into the repository:

```bash
npx @gohead-cms/client model pull
```

Review the diff, commit, and every environment can be set up the same way.

Pages are rendered once and cached. When content changes, GoHead sends a **signed webhook** to `/api/revalidate`, which checks the signature and revalidates the matching cache tags.

```ts
const event = await parseWebhook(request, process.env.GOHEAD_WEBHOOK_SECRET!);
if (!event) return new Response("invalid signature", { status: 401 });
revalidateTag(`gohead:${event.collection}`);
```

Without the webhook, pages still refresh: every request to GoHead is cached for a minute (`GOHEAD_REVALIDATE`).

Attributes marked `"localized": true` keep one value per locale. The starter reads them with the client's `locale` option:

```ts
const gohead = client.with({ locale: "fr" });
const article = await gohead.collection("articles").findFirst({ filters: { slug } });
```

Missing translations fall back to the default locale, so a half-translated site still works. Switch the language in the header to see it.
